{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Let them fall</b> — all of them into one trap, for all their thoughts and their secret." "<b>Together with me</b> — perhaps I will pass over the snare and it will be caught and I will be seized, in the manner of: 'and I, their deeds and their thoughts'; therefore the word יחד was joined with אנכי. And R. Moses the Cohen said: for the meaning is, let them fall together until I pass by, and they will not seize me."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 141, :notes {0 "The verse cited is Psalms 141:10, יפלו אליו במכמורים. The Hebrew ends abruptly after וסודם, 'and their secret,' with no predicate; translated hyper-literally to preserve the truncation.", 1 "The clause 'in the manner of: and I, their deeds and their thoughts' appears to quote a verse or paraphrase, but the reference is not specified; rendered as found."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:32.410999780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}